.TH "PB-TUNNEL-ROUTE-ADD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-route-add - Add a tunnel route


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel route add <tunnel> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a tunnel route

.PP
Add a route to one durable tunnel, selecting protocol, match, origin, and optional TLS behavior. The operation can remain connecting after the command returns; use --wait or status to confirm readiness.

.PP
Routes map a public or private match to a specific origin and protocol. TLS and host-header options affect the trust boundary and should match the origin. Adding or updating a route may return an operation whose readiness must be checked separately.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--clear-client-credential-reference\fP[=false]
	remove the origin mTLS credential reference

.PP
\fB--clear-host-header\fP[=false]
	remove the origin Host override

.PP
\fB--clear-tls-server-name\fP[=false]
	remove the explicit origin TLS server name

.PP
\fB--client-credential-reference\fP=""
	protected origin mTLS credential reference

.PP
\fB--connect-timeout\fP=10s
	origin connect timeout

.PP
\fB--domain\fP=""
	exact hostname or one-label wildcard match

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--host-header\fP=""
	override the origin Host header

.PP
\fB--idle-timeout\fP=5m0s
	stream idle timeout

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--max-streams\fP=1024
	maximum concurrent streams

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	name

.PP
\fB--path\fP=""
	HTTP path prefix, optionally ending in *

.PP
\fB--preserve-host\fP[=true]
	preserve the incoming Host header

.PP
\fB--priority\fP=0
	route priority

.PP
\fB--protocol\fP="http"
	route protocol (http, tcp, tls passthrough, or tcp_private)

.PP
\fB--redirect\fP=[]
	redirect a path prefix: '/from -> [301|302|307|308:]/to-or-https-URL' (repeatable, at most 4)

.PP
\fB--request-header\fP=[]
	request header rule op:Name=value (op add or set) or remove:Name, sent to the app (repeatable, at most 8)

.PP
\fB--response-header\fP=[]
	response header rule op:Name=value (op add or set) or remove:Name, sent to the visitor (repeatable, at most 8)

.PP
\fB--rewrite-path\fP=[]
	rewrite a path prefix before the app sees it: '/from -> /to'

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--tls-ca\fP=""
	trust this CA for the origin (PEM file, e.g. Caddy's tls internal root); sets custom_ca

.PP
\fB--tls-pin\fP=""
	pin the origin certificate by its fingerprint (sha256:<hex>), without connecting

.PP
\fB--tls-server-name\fP=""
	explicit origin TLS server name

.PP
\fB--tls-verification\fP=""
	origin TLS verification: system, custom_ca, pinned (shows the origin certificate and pins it), or insecure

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	to

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


